    tripShapes: [
      { title: '2 nights · one Canberra priority', copy: 'With two nights, arrival and departure are often partial days: protect one full day for Parliament House plus one Parkes institution, or choose a single other district if that is the trip’s priority. Add the National Museum or War Memorial only as a short arrival/departure block when the actual flight, coach and bus times leave enough margin. Route 53 serves the Museum corridor, R54 the Memorial stop, and Routes 57/58 Parliament House; verify both the outbound and return. If weather or mobility removes the optional outdoor walk, keep the indoor anchor. Leave Namadgi and Kosciuszko for a longer stay.' },
      { title: '4 nights · three city days', copy: 'Four nights usually allow three full Canberra days: Parliament House and one Parkes institution; the National Museum and a short West Basin walk; and the War Memorial with an optional Mount Ainslie approach. Check each day’s direction and final return on Routes 53, R54, 57 or 58 as relevant. If the summit route, ceremony timing or exposed paths do not fit, retain the indoor visit and skip the optional walk. Keep Namadgi outside this city schedule unless the group deliberately replaces one institutional day and arranges the park transport.' },
      { title: '5 nights · city plus a reserve day', copy: 'Use three full days for Parliament House and one other Parkes institution, the National Museum/West Basin, and the War Memorial with an optional summit. Keep the fourth full day for Namadgi only after checking ACT Parks alerts, fire status, road access, daylight and a suitable vehicle or confirmed operator; otherwise make it an indoor collection, rest or weather reserve. Do not treat that buffer as an alpine day trip to Jindabyne.' },
      { title: '8 nights · capital then alpine gateway', copy: 'Allow four Canberra nights for three full city days, then four nights in Jindabyne or the gateway that matches the chosen Kosciuszko area. Use the booked Canberra Civic–Jindabyne Route 775 coach or a suitable car and schedule the transfer as its own leg; confirm onward transport and accommodation before departure. Two mountain days plus one spare weather day fit only if local access is confirmed. Park entry, roads, chains, lifts and seasonal shuttles are separate from the regional coach. Verify the actual service dates, park alerts, road rules and exact trail or lift before fixing this high-country leg.' }
    ],
