      ['Can I visit the Snowy Mountains from a Canberra hotel?', 'Treat the move to Jindabyne as a regional transfer, not a convenient return day trip. NSW TrainLink lists a booked Canberra Civic–Jindabyne coach, but the onward trip from Jindabyne to the chosen park area needs its own current vehicle or operator plan.'],
      ['Which bus serves the Canberra institutions?', 'Transport Canberra’s current visitor routes guide lists Route 53 for the National Museum corridor and R54 for the War Memorial; Routes 57/58 serve Parliament House. Stops and schedules vary by direction and date, so plan the return as well as the arrival.'],
      ['Should I cross Lake Burley Griffin between city visits?', 'Treat a crossing as its own route choice. The active Commonwealth Avenue Bridge works affect the northbound road and shared path; check the National Capital Authority’s current diversion and use one district per day if the detour makes the return uncertain.'],
      ['What changes between Canberra and the alpine region?', 'Canberra museums and city buses operate on urban schedules. Namadgi depends on park, fire and road conditions; Kosciuszko needs a gateway, local transfer, season and mountain weather plan. Move your base before the alpine leg.'],
      ['Can I rely on winter transport in October?', 'No. The published 2026 Snowy Mountains Bus Service season ended on 4 October. Recheck the operator’s current season and timetable for your dates and arrange a separate onward option if it is not operating.']
